2.m:
I do not know the instruction for austerities, O best of sages;
if it is fitting for you, instruct me in this secret.
This is what I wish to do; there is no other secret.

bathing should be performed in silence, and worship too in silence;
food should consist of leaves and water at the first two sixth intervals;
and at the third sixth interval, one should be dedicated to fasting.

Thus, at the completion of austerities, the ritual takes place at the sixth interval;
and one should wear the bark of trees and sleep on the bare ground at that time.
Such practice of the vow, performed in silence and called penance, yields fruit.
